questions.workedExample:
Ask what a thread *is*: an independent sequence of execution. To run independently it needs:

1. its own program counter (where it is in the code);
2. its own registers;
3. its own **stack**, because each thread is in a different chain of function calls with different local variables.

Everything else (code, heap, globals, open files) belongs to the process and is shared. So the stack is the per-thread item.

questions.prompt:
Three threads each run `work()` once, concurrently. What does each thread print?

```c
#include <stdatomic.h>
atomic_int hits = 0;

void *work(void *arg) {
    int mine = 0;
    mine++;
    atomic_fetch_add(&hits, 1);
    printf("mine=%d\n", mine);
    return NULL;
}
```

What is the most likely result of running this program?

```c
void *hello(void *arg) {
    sleep(1);
    printf("hello\n");
    return NULL;
}

int main(void) {
    pthread_t t;
    pthread_create(&t, NULL,
                   hello, NULL);
    return 0;
}
```

questions.workedExample:
1. Classic Unix system calls return −1 and put the reason in `errno`.
2. The pthreads functions were designed differently: they **return the error number** itself and return 0 on success.
3. For a thread limit (`RLIMIT_NPROC`, `threads-max`) or lack of memory, `pthread_create` returns `EAGAIN`.

So write:

```c
int rc = pthread_create(...);
if (rc != 0)
    fprintf(stderr, "%s\n",
            strerror(rc));
```

questions.prompt:
What correctness problem does this code have?

```c
void *f(void *arg) {
    printf("%d\n", *(int *)arg);
    return NULL;
}

int main(void) {
    pthread_t t[4];
    int i;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++)
        pthread_create(&t[i], NULL,
                       f, &i);
    for (int j = 0; j < 4; j++)
        pthread_join(t[j], NULL);
}
```

Assume 64-byte cache lines, 8-byte long, distinct valid me values and repeated memory accesses as shown. Which cache-coherence problem can make this four-thread loop slower?

```c
_Alignas(64) volatile long counts[4];

void *work(void *arg) {
    int me = *(int *)arg;
    for (long i = 0; i < 100000000;
         i++)
        counts[me]++;
    return NULL;
}
```

